# statusgen + desk-tools pins for the adopter-scaffold example.
#
# This is the file an adopting repo commits so its CI (and a local install) can
# fetch KNOWN binaries and verify them byte-for-byte before running them. A pinned
# sha256 is the one thing a re-tagged release cannot silently swap out.
#
# The umbrella line (`assay vX.Y.Z`, no sha256) names a COMPOSITION — which
# per-artifact tags make up that suite version (see releases/<umbrella>.yaml). It
# is what `deskversion` / `upgrade-assay` read to know which suite version this
# tree is on.
#
# ONE TAG, ONE TREE (derived-board §6): every ARTIFACT line carries the SAME tag —
# statusgen and desk-tools read one tree and must not straddle two schema
# boundaries. `statusgen --lint` PROBLEMs an .assay-versions whose artifact tags
# differ.
#
